      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your throat tightness and facial swelling are classic signs of a severe allergic reaction, not a minor nuisance, and you must take an EpiPen immediately if you have one. If you don't have an EpiPen, you need to go to the ER right now because your airway could close within minutes, and Benadryl alone is too slow to save your life. Do not try to sleep it off or save money; the cost of an ER visit is nothing compared to the risk of choking or dying from anaphylaxis.",
